{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Who did not meet you.</b> Both of them did not meet you, but Moab did give bread and water for silver, as it says: ״אֹכֶל בַּכֶּסֶף תַּשְׁבִּרֵנִי וגו׳ כַּאֲשֶׁר עָשׂוּ לִי בְנֵי עֵשָׂו הַיֹּשְׁבִים בְּשֵׂעִיר וְהַמּוֹאָבִים הַיֹּשְׁבִים בְּעָר״ (Deuteronomy 2:28–29). But the Ammonites did not do so. However, Moab added to its sin the transgression of ״who hired against you״ (Deuteronomy 23:5). Thus ״you shall not seek their peace״ (Deuteronomy 23:7) applies to both, because both did not meet you — and Ammon did not give even for silver, while Moab, who did give, hired Balaam."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:03.536621716Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}